      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Matter"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Matter is anything that occupies space and possesses mass.",
        "Matter exists primarily in solid, liquid, and gaseous states.",
        "Changes in the states of matter occur due to alterations in temperature and pressure.",
        "Density is a fundamental physical property defined as mass per unit volume.",
        "Elasticity measures the tendency of a material to resume its original shape after deformation.",
        "Pressure measures the perpendicular force exerted per unit surface area."
      ],
      "id": "iun798k"
